":false},\"body\":\"CheckpointMetadataRef() currently returns primaryCheckpointRef(), which is \\\"entire/checkpoints/v1\\\" in legacy mode. Several tests use this value with `git show-ref --verify` / `git rev-parse --verify` to assert that the checkpoint ref is missing/present locally, but those commands either require a fully-qualified ref (show-ref) or may DWIM-resolve to `refs/remotes/origin/entire/checkpoints/v1` in fresh clones (rev-parse), making the assertions unreliable. Consider returning the exact local refname in legacy mode (e.g. `refs/heads/entire/checkpoints/v1`) and keeping v2 as `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main`, or adding a separate helper specifically for local verification.\\n```suggestion\\n// CheckpointMetadataRef returns the exact local metadata ref name used by the\\n// active suite mode. Tests use this to verify local fetch-on-demand behavior\\n// without relying on ambiguous DWIM ref resolution.\\nfunc CheckpointMetadataRef() string {\\n\\tswitch checkpointsMode() {\\n\\tcase checkpointsModeLegacy:\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"refs/heads/\\\" + checkpointRefV1\\n\\tcase checkpointsModeV2DualWrite, checkpointsModeV2Only:\\n\\t\\treturn checkpointRefV2Main\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"refs/heads/\\\" + checkpointRefV1\\n\\t}\\n```\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-23T00:59:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-23T00:59:40Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1012#discussion_r3127728122\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1012\",\"_links\":{\"self\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/comments/3127728122\"},\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1012#discussion_r3127728122\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1012\"}},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/entirei…12878 chars truncated…users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api